WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.700
Unit 3 is the attribute,
pim and the perimeter.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:05.240
Under dynamic membership,

3
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:08.925
whoever can write the attribute
a rule reads controls access.

4
00:00:08.925 --> 00:00:13.883
So the book's Chapter 17 has rules read
H R owned codes, such as the organization

5
00:00:13.883 --> 00:00:18.687
code in extension attribute ten, never
display strings such as department.

6
00:00:18.687 --> 00:00:22.213
And every access rule excludes
disabled accounts and guests.

7
00:00:22.213 --> 00:00:24.937
Groups that hold sys-admin
are never dynamic.

8
00:00:24.937 --> 00:00:28.799
Microsoft Learn says pim for Groups
doesn't work on dynamic groups,

9
00:00:28.799 --> 00:00:31.326
or on groups synchronized
from on premises.

10
00:00:31.326 --> 00:00:34.325
So privileged groups are
cloud-only and assigned.

11
00:00:34.325 --> 00:00:38.373
Otherwise, whoever can write the
attribute could make someone sys-admin.

12
00:00:38.373 --> 00:00:41.612
Conditional Access then sits
in front of every user token.

13
00:00:41.612 --> 00:00:45.931
But it applies to users, not to
managed identities, so applications are

14
00:00:45.931 --> 00:00:50.400
covered by the application chain in
Chapter 7, not by Conditional Access.
